---

<InstagramEmbeds />

<div class="smg-header-collage" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div class="smg-page">
  <section class="smg-hero" id="top">
    <div class="smg-hero__copy">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Vintage Gibson Specialist</p>
      <h1>Sell Your Vintage Gibson to a Buyer Who Knows What It Is</h1>
      <p class="smg-hero__lead">Send me a few photos and tell me what you know about the guitar. I'll look it over myself and, if it's a guitar I can buy, make you a cash offer with no obligation.</p>
      <div class="smg-hero__actions">
        <Button href="#appraisal" variant="rust" size="lg">Get a Free Appraisal</Button>
        <a class="smg-button-secondary" href={hrefs.tel}>Call or Text Joe</a>
      </div>
      <div class="smg-trust-row">
        <span>Insured Nationwide Shipping</span>
        <span>No Obligation</span>
        <span>Deal Directly With Joe</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="smg-hero__image">
      <LicensedImage src={heroGuitar} alt="Vintage 1957 Gibson Les Paul Goldtop handled by Joe's Vintage Guitars" width={950} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-proof" aria-label="Joe's experience">
    <div><strong>12+</strong><span>Years Buying Full-Time</span></div>
    <div><strong>10,000+</strong><span>Instruments Appraised</span></div>
    <div><strong>50</strong><span>States Bought From</span></div>
    <div><strong>2,100+</strong><span>Positive Reviews</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-process" id="process">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="how-to-sell-your-guitar"></span>
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="my-guitar-buying-process"></span>
    <header class="smg-heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">How It Works</p>
      <h2>Selling Your Gibson Doesn't Have to Be Complicated</h2>
      <p>You'll deal with me from the first message through payment. Here's what I need to get started.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-steps">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Send Me Photos</h3><p>Take clear photos of the front, back, headstock, serial number and case. Please don't clean or repair the guitar first.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>I'll Look It Over</h3><p>I'll identify the guitar and check the details that affect its value. There's no charge for the appraisal.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>I'll Make an Offer</h3><p>If it's a guitar I can buy, I'll make you a cash offer. You're free to accept it or turn it down.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Review the Complete Handoff</h3><p>If shipping is the best option, I explain it with the offer so you can consider the full process before deciding.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-shipping" id="shipping">
    <div class="smg-shipping__intro">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Nationwide Shipping</p>
      <h2>A Simple, Proven Way to Ship Your Vintage Gibson</h2>
      <p>Sellers across the country have trusted me with valuable and sentimental guitars. If we can't meet in person, I explain the shipping process with the offer so you can consider everything before deciding.</p>
      <p>We agree on the shipping and payment details before the guitar moves, and I stay available throughout the process.</p>
      <div class="smg-shipping__included"><strong>There's no shipping cost to you.</strong> Through my special FedEx account, the box, professional packing, fully insured shipping and tracking are all provided at the FedEx location.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="smg-shipping__columns">
      <article><h3>What You Receive With the Offer</h3><ul><li>A clear explanation of the process</li><li>Shipping and insurance details</li><li>Payment timing and options</li></ul></article>
      <article><h3>What I Handle if You Decide to Sell</h3><ul><li>Prepaid shipping arrangements</li><li>Transit coverage and tracking</li><li>Communication through the handoff</li></ul></article>
    </div>
    <div class="smg-shipping__evidence">
      <header><p class="smg-eyebrow">From Sellers Who Used the Process</p><h3>Read What Sellers Said</h3><p>These comments come from people who shipped guitars to me. Each one links to the original Google review.</p></header>
      <div class="smg-shipping__reviews">
        {shippingReviews.map((review) => (
          <a href={review.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="smg-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
            <blockquote>“{review.quote}”</blockquote>
            <strong>{review.name}</strong>
            <small>Read the Google Review</small>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-value" id="value">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="how-much-is-my-gibson-guitar"></span>
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="find-out-gibson-really-worth"></span>
    <header class="smg-heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">How I Appraise a Gibson</p>
      <h2>What Affects the Value of a Vintage Gibson?</h2>
      <p>A serial number helps me start, but it doesn't tell the whole story. I look at these six areas together.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-value__grid">
      {values.map((item) => (
        <article>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={item.icon}></path></svg>
          <h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="smg-section-link">For more detail, read how the <a href="/post/how-the-year-of-manufacture-of-your-vintage-gibson-guitar-affects-its-price/">year affects vintage Gibson value</a>, review <a href="/post/gibson-shipping-totals-1948-1979/">Gibson production totals</a>, or send me photos for a <a href="/free-appraisal/">free appraisal</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-photo-guide">
    <div>
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Before You Contact Me</p>
      <h2>Six Photographs That Help Me Identify Your Gibson</h2>
      <p>Use natural light and take the photos straight on. You don't need to remove pickups, open the electronics or take anything apart.</p>
      <a class="smg-text-link" href="/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/">Use My Gibson Dating Guide</a>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><strong>Full Front</strong><small>Include the entire body and headstock.</small></li>
      <li><span>02</span><strong>Full Back</strong><small>Show the neck, body and any wear or repairs.</small></li>
      <li><span>03</span><strong>Headstock Front</strong><small>Keep the logo, tuners and truss-rod cover in view.</small></li>
      <li><span>04</span><strong>Headstock Back</strong><small>Photograph the serial number and factory stamps clearly.</small></li>
      <li><span>05</span><strong>Bridge and Controls</strong><small>Show the pickups, knobs, bridge and tailpiece.</small></li>
      <li><span>06</span><strong>Case and Paperwork</strong><small>Include tags, receipts, old parts and family photos.</small></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-owner-stories" id="owner-stories">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="consider-selling-your-guitar"></span>
    <header class="smg-heading smg-owner-stories__heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Guitars I've Bought</p>
      <h2>Original Owners and the Stories Behind Their Gibsons</h2>
      <p>These Gibsons arrived with the names, photographs and memories of the people who played them. I preserve those stories so they can travel with the instruments.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-owner-grid">
      {ownerStories.map((story) => (
        <a class="smg-owner-card" href={story.url}>
          <div class="smg-owner-card__image"><LicensedImage src={story.image} alt={story.imageAlt} width={620} loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="smg-owner-card__copy"><span>{story.detail}</span><h3>{story.title}</h3><p>{story.summary}</p><small>Read the Complete Story</small></div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-owner-videos" aria-labelledby="social-proof-title">
    <header class="smg-heading">
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Original Owners and Families on Video</p>
      <h2 id="social-proof-title">Watch the Stories Behind the Guitars</h2>
      <p>These short videos feature original owners, their families and the histories they shared when the guitars came to me.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="smg-video-grid">
      {socialPosts.map((post) => (
        <article class="smg-video-card">
          <div class="smg-video-card__story"><h3>{post.title}</h3><p>{post.story}</p></div>
          <div class="smg-video-card__embed">
            <blockquote class="instagram-media" data-instgrm-permalink={`https://www.instagram.com/reel/${post.id}/`} data-instgrm-version="14"></blockquote>
          </div>
          <a href={`https://www.instagram.com/reel/${post.id}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View This Video on Instagram</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <a class="smg-follow-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/joesvintageguitarsaz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch More Guitar Stories on Instagram</a>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-meet" id="meet-connoisseur-joe-dampt">
    <figure><LicensedImage src={joePhoto} alt="Joe Dampt playing a Gibson guitar" width={720} loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <div>
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Meet the Buyer</p>
      <h2>I'm Joe Dampt</h2>
      <p>I've spent more than twelve years buying vintage guitars full-time and have appraised more than 10,000 instruments. When you send a Gibson to Joe's Vintage Guitars, I'm the person who looks at it.</p>
      <p>I pay attention to the things that separate one Gibson from another: the finish, pickups, electronics, hardware, repairs and the story that came with it. If I can buy your guitar, I'll explain what I see and make you an offer.</p>
      <a class="smg-text-link" href="/about-me/">Learn More About Joe</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-preservation">
    <figure><LicensedImage src={byrdlandPhoto} alt="Original owner Don Majure with his sunburst 1957 Gibson Byrdland" width={820} loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <div>
      <p class="smg-eyebrow">Keeping the Story With the Guitar</p>
      <h2>The Photographs and Names Matter Too</h2>
      <p>When a guitar comes with family photos or a story about its owner, I keep those materials with it. I often print the story and place it inside the case so the next owner knows who played the guitar before them.</p>
      <p>If you inherited a Gibson, don't worry if you don't know the model or year. Keep the case, old parts, receipts and photographs together, then send me what you have.</p>
      <a class="smg-text-link" href="/post/one-owner-1957-gibson-byrdland/">Read the One-Owner Byrdland Story</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-expertise">
    <div><p class="smg-eyebrow">Research Your Guitar</p><h2>A Serial Number Is Only the Beginning</h2></div>
    <div><p>The serial number should agree with the construction and parts on the guitar. When those clues don't match, I take a closer look.</p><p>Start with my <a href="/how-to-read-gibson-serial-numbers/">Gibson serial-number guide</a>, compare <a href="/post/gibson-paf-patent-number-pickup-guide/">PAF and Patent Number pickups</a>, or check the <a href="/post/gibson-shipping-totals-1948-1979/">Gibson production totals</a>.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-options" id="best-way-to-sell">
    <header class="smg-heading"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Know Your Options</p><h2>Should You Sell to a Dealer, Consign It or Sell It Yourself?</h2><p>There's no single right answer. It depends on whether you care most about speed, convenience, control or the highest possible retail price.</p></header>
    <div class="smg-options__table" role="table" aria-label="Ways to sell a vintage Gibson">
      <div class="smg-options__row smg-options__head" role="row"><strong role="columnheader">Option</strong><strong role="columnheader">Why People Choose It</strong><strong role="columnheader">What to Consider</strong></div>
      <div class="smg-options__row" role="row"><strong role="cell">Sell Directly to Me</strong><span role="cell">A cash offer, no public listing and help with the handoff.</span><span role="cell">I pay among the highest dealer prices, but my offer will still be a little below the guitar's full retail market value.</span></div>
      <div class="smg-options__row" role="row"><strong role="cell">Consignment</strong><span role="cell">You may receive more if the guitar sells at the asking price.</span><span role="cell">You pay a commission and may wait weeks or months for a buyer.</span></div>
      <div class="smg-options__row" role="row"><strong role="cell">Auction</strong><span role="cell">Several bidders can compete for a rare or well-known guitar.</span><span role="cell">The final price is uncertain, and seller fees, photography and shipping still matter.</span></div>
      <div class="smg-options__row" role="row"><strong role="cell">Private Listing</strong><span role="cell">You control the asking price and speak directly with buyers.</span><span role="cell">You handle questions, negotiation, fraud risk, returns, packing and insurance.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-wanted">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="receive-the-highest-payout"></span>
    <div><p class="smg-eyebrow">Gibsons I Buy</p><h2>Vintage Electric, Acoustic and Carved-Top Gibsons</h2><p>I'm always looking for clean, original and unusual Gibsons. I also buy guitars with changed parts or old repairs, so please ask before ruling yours out.</p><a class="smg-text-link" href="#appraisal">Tell Me About Your Gibson</a></div>
    <ul>{wantedModels.map((model) => (<li>{model}</li>))}</ul>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-guides" id="guitar-families">
    <header class="smg-heading"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Gibson Models I Know</p><h2>Start With the Family Your Guitar Belongs To</h2><p>These guides cover the solid-body, thinline, acoustic and Gibson archtop families owners contact me about most often.</p></header>
    <div class="smg-guide-grid">
      {modelGuides.map((guide) => (
        <article class="smg-guide-card">
          <span>{guide.detail}</span>
          <h3><a href={guide.url}>{guide.title}</a></h3>
          <a class="smg-guide-card__primary" href={guide.url}>{guide.action}</a>
          {guide.more && <div class="smg-guide-card__more">{guide.more.map(([label, url]) => (<a href={url}>{label}</a>))}</div>}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <a class="smg-all-guides" href="/blog/">Browse All Guitar Articles</a>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-reviews" id="our-clients-testimonials">
    <header class="smg-heading"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Reviews From Sellers</p><h2>What People Say After Selling Me a Guitar</h2><p>These reviews are from people who sold guitars to me. Click any one to read the original review on Google.</p></header>
    <div class="smg-review-grid">
      {reviews.map((review) => (
        <a class="smg-review-card" href={review.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <span class="smg-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
          <blockquote>“{review.quote}”</blockquote><strong>{review.name}</strong><span>{review.detail}</span><small>Read the Google Review</small>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-section smg-faq" id="faqs-about-gibson">
    <header class="smg-heading"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Questions Gibson Owners Ask Me</p><h2>Before You Sell a Vintage Gibson</h2><p>You don't need to identify or clean the guitar before contacting me. Send what you know, and I'll help with the rest.</p></header>
    <div class="smg-faq__list">
      {faqs.map((item, index) => (<details open={index === 0}><summary>{item.q}</summary><p>{item.a}</p></details>))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="smg-appraisal" id="appraisal">
    <span class="smg-anchor" id="receive-free-consultation"></span>
    <div class="smg-appraisal__copy"><p class="smg-eyebrow">Talk With Me</p><h2>Tell Me About Your Gibson</h2><p>Share what you know and send a few photos. I'll look at the guitar myself and get back to you.</p><a href={hrefs.tel}>Call or Text {contact.phone}</a></div>
    <LeadForm formId="sell-my-gibson" instrumentMode="model-only" serial={{ label: "What does the serial number look like? Look on the back of the headstock or inside the body.", options: serialOptions }} submitLabel="Send" />
  </section>
</div>

